{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 never appears on ser_tx; sim ends with uart timeout, no byte received (FAIL 0xdead vs expected RX 0xa5). ser_tx stays idle because send_pattern is repeatedly reloaded with ~0. Root cause in excerpt line 123: send_dummy <= 1 never clears the dummy-preamble state, so send_dummy && !send_bitcnt always wins over reg_dat_we and the TX engine loops 15 idle bits forever.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 			if (send_dummy && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= ~0;
 				send_bitcnt <= 15;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
-				send_dummy <= 1;
+				send_dummy <= 0;
 			end else
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
", "expected": "tohost PASS with loopback byte 0xa5 received, no uart timeout"}

